 "_doc": [
  "TNPCB's laboratory samples of the Thenpennai at Chokkarasanapalli village, the river's entry point into Tamil Nadu (interstate border, Hosur taluk), transcribed from the reports of analysis TNPCB filed before the NGT (Southern Zone). The tables were read from the page images; every value is as printed.",
  "Conventions: a value printed with an asterisk (for example '1.0*') is the laboratory's detection limit with the sample below it; '<MDL' is below the minimum detection limit with no limit printed; null is a '-' or '----' cell; 'illegible' is a glyph that cannot be read on the page.",
  "Gaps: no samples are filed for May 2021 to March 2025. For 2022-23 and 2023-24 TNPCB reported ranges only (see 'rangesAsReported'). The 'tnpcbUnit' column below names the laboratory the sheet credits.",
  "The position is CPCB's NWMP station 'Thenpennaiyar at Chokkarasanahalli bridge' as the National Water Data Portal prints it (12.863435, 77.831855), which plots 30 m from the mapped river and 110 m inside the district line; TNPCB's own sheets give no coordinates. NWDP tags that station to Dharmapuri district."
 ],
